course: dictionary
lesson: 15843
title: Undisputed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undisputed means nobody argues about it. Its parts help: un- means not, and disputed means argued about. «She is the undisputed champion of the school chess club.» Nobody argues that she is the best, so her title is clear.
explain: The word also means certainly true and not questioned. «It is an undisputed fact that the Earth goes round the Sun.» Experts agree on this, so nobody needs to check it or argue about it.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try «the champion everyone agrees on» in place of «the undisputed champion». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Undisputed means accepted by everyone, so no one argues about it.
fact: «The undisputed king of the playground» is the child everyone agrees is the leader.
fact: Undisputed can also mean certainly true and not questioned.
fact: «An undisputed fact» is one that all experts agree on.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in unhappy and unkind, so look for it when you meet a long word.
exercise: «The team won every game, so she is the undisputed champion.» What does undisputed mean here? | *Accepted by everyone, with no argument | Very small | Lost and forgotten | Argued about by everyone
exercise: Ben says, «It is an undisputed fact that water boils when it gets hot enough.» What does undisputed suggest? | *Certainly true and not questioned | Hard to say | Made up by a child | Only sometimes true
exercise: «The queen's place as leader was undisputed.» Find and copy the word that means not argued about. | place | leader | queen | *undisputed
test: «Everyone agrees he is the undisputed best reader in our class.» What does undisputed mean here? | Argued about by many people | *Accepted by everyone, with no argument | Hidden from the class | Written down in a book
test: Mia asks, «Is an undisputed fact something people still argue about?» What is the answer? | Only in science lessons | Sometimes, but nobody knows when | Yes, it is always argued about | *No, everyone accepts it and it is not questioned
exam: Which sentence uses undisputed correctly? | He undisputed his lunch | The dog was undisputed in the park | The rain was undisputed by the umbrella | *Nobody argued that she was the undisputed winner
